# Artifact Contracts bind a content_hash to a repo:// path, so the bytes Git stores for a
# file must not depend on which platform cloned it. `text=auto` makes Git normalise every
# detected text blob to LF regardless of a contributor's local core.autocrlf setting, which
# is the canonical representation studio_core/integrity.py hashes against.
* text=auto

# Binary assets must never be line-ending normalised: studio_core/integrity.py hashes their
# raw bytes, and Git must store them the same way.
#
# SYS-AST-0014: every extension on the policies/binary-assets.yaml allowlist must appear below
# with `binary` or `-text`. studio_core/binary_assets.py cross-checks the two and fails the
# baseline if an allowed extension is not pinned here -- an unpinned extension would let Git's
# `* text=auto` rewrite CRLF inside an asset, so the committed blob and the raw bytes the
# manifest declares would no longer be the same thing. Extensions listed here but absent from
# the policy allowlist stay refused by the gate; this file widens nothing on its own.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.wav binary
*.ogg binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
